# 0014 in-game inventory A/B - how much of the game's memory 0014 moves back
# to tiled, measured on the device (RE4, DX12 via vkd3d-proton).
#
# Method. experiments/exp-14-image-inventory.patch prints one line per created
# image (format, width, height, samples, tiling, size). It is a measurement
# patch, it is not part of the driver. The sample is a fixed protocol: game
# boot -> load the save -> walk the depot corridor -> sit in the inventory for
# 180 s (this is where the game allocates the render scale targets) -> quit.
# The same path was walked on both builds, 2 samples per build; the two
# samples of a build agree to ~3%, and the effect below is 57%, so one sample
# per build is enough to state the number.
#
# Only 'mutable, no format list' images are counted, because those are what
# 0014 changes. scripts/fmt-list-gate-check.py --no-list classifies every
# image of a raw log by the same rule the driver uses, and reports the
# 'deposed' set: images the driver put in linear although their class would be
# allowed tiled. The difference between the two runs is what the class answer
# moved to tiled.
#
# The raw logs (results/raw/) are NOT committed: a log of this run is ~1 MB of
# device output tied to one specific save file and one specific session. They
# are on disk next to this file. The classifier and the experiment patch are
# committed, so the number can be re-measured.
#
#   baseline  2026-11-18 build, stock no-list answer, imginv4
#             raw: results/raw/game-patched-imginv4.log
#   candidate build 050375a18b7b (0013+0014), imginv5
#             raw: results/raw/game-patched-imginv5.log
#
# HUD window 40-50 s of the same session (HUDINTERVAL=100): baseline
# clocks=[220] fps p25 10.2 gpu_load 73%; candidate clocks=[220, 670] fps p25
# 15.4 gpu_load 88%. Recorded for completeness only: the fps of this game
# turned out to be dominated by GPU clock ramping, not by layout (see
# docs/fdperf-a7xx.md), so this row is not the proof of 0014 - the byte-exact
# matrix and the memory number are.


